<title>USA: Exxon says minor oil output loss due storm.</title>
<headline>Exxon says minor oil output loss due storm.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp said Friday that it had suffered only minor production loss from its offshore operations due to Hurricane Danny.</p>
<p>&quot;We have experienced only minor production losses. Onshore facilities at Grand Isle, La. have experienced some coastal flooding but operations are being maintained,&quot; said Exxon in a statement.</p>
<p>The company's 432,000 barrels per day refinery in Baton Rouge, La. is taking precautionary measures for high windes but operations are uncaffected by the storm, Exxon said.</p>
</text>
